- **E8 ran.** Array 53931130: 34 tasks, 3 runs packed per task (the same `vit_jepa.py`, 9,750 steps per run), all COMPLETED, none near the 2 h limit. Task time was 42-56 min on the `gpu` partition nodes (the registered 50-60 min) and 17-27 min on `gpu4` nodes. Sum of task Elapsed is **23.5 GPU-h for 100 runs, 0.235 GPU-h per run**; the longest task was 55.7 min. All 34 tasks started within 56 min of submission; the 8-task `e8ref` array took 15-22 min per task.
- **E7 pilots** 53937878/53937879: 3 epochs, 3 runs packed, 3 min 35 s - 3 min 40 s each (`gpu` partition), consistent with the registered 168-185 s of training plus start-up.
- **E7 projection.** 55 runs = 19 tasks (18 of 3 runs, one of 1). At the slow-node rate (55 min per full task) that is 18 x 0.93 + 0.4 = **~17.2 GPU-h**; at the E8 average rate (0.235 per run) it is ~13. The registered ~17 is therefore the upper end, not an optimistic figure, and the bound of 20 leaves ~15% margin over the slow case.
